# Reviewer-owned over-budget grants: `<path> <one-clause reason>` per line. An
# accepted file drops out of the `bench structure` count and prints in the
# `accepted:` section with its reason. `#` starts a comment; a row with no reason
# is ignored as malformed; a path that is no longer a scanned source file is
# reported stale. Exact paths only — a grant is a named, reversible decision, not
# a threshold bump.
internal/status/status.go cohesive severity-ladder renderer; barely over budget and splitting would fragment one signal
internal/contract/runtime/runtime_status_test.go cohesive status-contract family; barely over budget and shares one fixture harness
internal/contract/runtime/ one contract package per command family sharing a single fixture harness; regrouping into subpackages would duplicate the harness
internal/contract/surface/link_test.go cohesive link-contract family; barely over budget after the dist-gitignore case
internal/conformance/ cohesive conformance-check family; the shipped-surface sweep earns its own file, and the dir sits one over a full budget rather than fragmenting a signal
